================================================================================
Source material — OWASP Agentic Skills Top 10
================================================================================

The OWASP Agentic Skills Top 10 whitepaper, version 1.0, is the SOURCE MATERIAL
for this repository, and this repository implements that edition and no other.
It is published at
https://owasp.org/www-project-agentic-skills-top-10/assets/publications/ast10-top10-whitepaper-2.pdf

Every category (AST01-AST10), every attack scenario enumerated in
scenarios/registry.yaml, the "Which AST Does My Finding Belong To?" decision
tree implemented by skills/advisory, and the Universal Skill Format proposal
validated by validators/usf.py and schemas/usf-v1.schema.json originate in that
publication. They are adopted here, not invented here. Verbatim scenario titles
are reproduced for identification and traceability.

Ken Huang (DistributedApps.ai, https://github.com/kenhuangus) is the project
leader of the OWASP Agentic Skills Top 10 and originated the taxonomy and the
source repository.

THIS REPOSITORY IS NOT AN OWASP PROJECT. It is an independent community
implementation and carries no OWASP endorsement, review, or affiliation,
despite the repository name. Jacky Chan (https://github.com/jhkchan), the maintainer of this
repository, is a credited entry in the whitepaper's "Reviewers and
Contributors" table; that
is contributor credit on the publication, and is not authorship of it, not
leadership of the project, and not a mandate to implement it. Nothing here is
OWASP guidance. Where this repository and the whitepaper disagree, the
whitepaper is authoritative.

